            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53612",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program when applying post-mount ownership/mode changes"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. When an /etc/fstab entry uses the user option together with X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, or X-mount.mode, mount(8) changes ownership or permissions on the mount target after mounting without re-verifying the path. A local unprivileged user can exploit this Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) window by swapping the target directory, redirecting the ownership/permission change to an arbitrary file and potentially escalating privileges to root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53612",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53612\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: util-linux\nFixed Version: 2.41.5-0+deb13u1\nLink: [CVE-2026-53612](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53612)\nA flaw was found in util-linux. When an /etc/fstab entry uses the user option together with X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, or X-mount.mode, mount(8) changes ownership or permissions on the mount target after mounting without re-verifying the path. A local unprivileged user can exploit this Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) window by swapping the target directory, redirecting the ownership/permission change to an arbitrary file and potentially escalating privileges to root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53612**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|util-linux|2.41.5-0+deb13u1|[CVE-2026-53612](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53612)|\n\nA flaw was found in util-linux. When an /etc/fstab entry uses the user option together with X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, or X-mount.mode, mount(8) changes ownership or permissions on the mount target after mounting without re-verifying the path. A local unprivileged user can exploit this Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) window by swapping the target directory, redirecting the ownership/permission change to an arbitrary file and potentially escalating privileges to root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53613",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program via ancestor directory swap on target path"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When an /etc/fstab entry is configured with the user or users option, mount(8) validates the target path before performing the mount syscall, creating a Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) window. A local unprivileged user with write access to an ancestor directory of the mount target can swap that directory to redirect the mount to an arbitrary root-owned location, potentially escalating privileges to root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53613",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53613\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: util-linux\nFixed Version: 2.41.5-0+deb13u1\nLink: [CVE-2026-53613](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53613)\nWhen an /etc/fstab entry is configured with the user or users option, mount(8) validates the target path before performing the mount syscall, creating a Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) window. A local unprivileged user with write access to an ancestor directory of the mount target can swap that directory to redirect the mount to an arbitrary root-owned location, potentially escalating privileges to root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53613**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|util-linux|2.41.5-0+deb13u1|[CVE-2026-53613](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53613)|\n\nWhen an /etc/fstab entry is configured with the user or users option, mount(8) validates the target path before performing the mount syscall, creating a Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use (TOCTOU) window. A local unprivileged user with write access to an ancestor directory of the mount target can swap that directory to redirect the mount to an arbitrary root-owned location, potentially escalating privileges to root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53614",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: SUID mount(8) allows nosuid/noexec bypass via LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. The mount(8) SUID binary does not sanitize the LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 environment variable before use. A local unprivileged user can set this variable to force mount(8) to use the legacy two-step mount(2) code path, which applies security restrictions such as nosuid and noexec after the mount is already active. During this window, an attacker can execute a SUID binary from the mounted filesystem, allowing local privilege escalation to root."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53614",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53614\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: util-linux\nFixed Version: 2.41.5-0+deb13u1\nLink: [CVE-2026-53614](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53614)\nA flaw was found in util-linux. The mount(8) SUID binary does not sanitize the LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 environment variable before use. A local unprivileged user can set this variable to force mount(8) to use the legacy two-step mount(2) code path, which applies security restrictions such as nosuid and noexec after the mount is already active. During this window, an attacker can execute a SUID binary from the mounted filesystem, allowing local privilege escalation to root.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53614**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|util-linux|2.41.5-0+deb13u1|[CVE-2026-53614](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53614)|\n\nA flaw was found in util-linux. The mount(8) SUID binary does not sanitize the LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 environment variable before use. A local unprivileged user can set this variable to force mount(8) to use the legacy two-step mount(2) code path, which applies security restrictions such as nosuid and noexec after the mount is already active. During this window, an attacker can execute a SUID binary from the mounted filesystem, allowing local privilege escalation to root."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-76642",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: failed external mount helper still runs privileged X-mount post-hooks"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux versions through 2.41.5 and 2.42.2 fail to check mount helper exit status before running post-mount hooks, allowing unprivileged users to execute privileged operations on pre-existing filesystems. Attackers can exploit X-mount.idmap or X-mount.owner hooks to clone filesystems with inherited suid bits or modify target inode permissions after a helper fails, achieving privilege escalation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-76642",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-76642\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: util-linux\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-76642](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-76642)\nutil-linux versions through 2.41.5 and 2.42.2 fail to check mount helper exit status before running post-mount hooks, allowing unprivileged users to execute privileged operations on pre-existing filesystems. Attackers can exploit X-mount.idmap or X-mount.owner hooks to clone filesystems with inherited suid bits or modify target inode permissions after a helper fails, achieving privilege escalation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-76642**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|util-linux||[CVE-2026-76642](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-76642)|\n\nutil-linux versions through 2.41.5 and 2.42.2 fail to check mount helper exit status before running post-mount hooks, allowing unprivileged users to execute privileged operations on pre-existing filesystems. Attackers can exploit X-mount.idmap or X-mount.owner hooks to clone filesystems with inherited suid bits or modify target inode permissions after a helper fails, achieving privilege escalation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
